/*
:name: spec_types_backtick_banned_params
:type: comptime
:verifier_pass: 2
:verifier_fail: 0
*/
// SPEC qa.md appendix section 8: "a backticked banned/reserved word (`u8`, `bool`, `U8`, `_0`, `_`) is an
// ordinary name". Rule: backticked banned words work as a parameter, an output and a named argument.
comb f(`u8`:U8) -> (`bool`:Bool) { `bool` = `u8` == 3 }
cassert(f(`u8`=3))
cassert(not f(`u8`=4))
